[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186119808 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c391d9c3-0c76-5e6f-b0c3-d6b4ee2c37cb" "question-a8427e64-b547-5ecb-a62e-824aa188b632" "question-ddfb229d-f01d-542c-8a6c-f2e9a5996154"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-c391d9c3-0c76-5e6f-b0c3-d6b4ee2c37cb" :question/id #uuid "c391d9c3-0c76-5e6f-b0c3-d6b4ee2c37cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-105199" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=3 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=3 \\\\ {x}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}+2{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=3\\cdot 2=6.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7847d689-0e36-5ac4-b435-bd1cf0642bc0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7847d689-0e36-5ac4-b435-bd1cf0642bc0" :answer-field/id #uuid "7847d689-0e36-5ac4-b435-bd1cf0642bc0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-98c56786-6605-5401-b672-c63cb1cecd33" :answer-field/choices ["answer-976c158b-03de-5101-af86-c772a635e855" "answer-38fb4394-142f-596a-acba-652af141f7ea" "answer-1f1cbd99-3722-58a8-94e3-9b80df51c48b" "answer-1442cd36-01ab-57b5-b752-7b7131e887f9" "answer-98c56786-6605-5401-b672-c63cb1cecd33"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-976c158b-03de-5101-af86-c772a635e855" :answer/id #uuid "976c158b-03de-5101-af86-c772a635e855" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-38fb4394-142f-596a-acba-652af141f7ea" :answer/id #uuid "38fb4394-142f-596a-acba-652af141f7ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f1cbd99-3722-58a8-94e3-9b80df51c48b" :answer/id #uuid "1f1cbd99-3722-58a8-94e3-9b80df51c48b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1442cd36-01ab-57b5-b752-7b7131e887f9" :answer/id #uuid "1442cd36-01ab-57b5-b752-7b7131e887f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-98c56786-6605-5401-b672-c63cb1cecd33" :answer/id #uuid "98c56786-6605-5401-b672-c63cb1cecd33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a8427e64-b547-5ecb-a62e-824aa188b632" :question/id #uuid "a8427e64-b547-5ecb-a62e-824aa188b632" :question/math-academy-id "q-34114" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=2 \\\\ {x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}+(-1){a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+(-1)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=2\\cdot (-1)=-2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-283164aa-73de-5dcd-8a69-e6c9e6374abc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-283164aa-73de-5dcd-8a69-e6c9e6374abc" :answer-field/id #uuid "283164aa-73de-5dcd-8a69-e6c9e6374abc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-35881d2a-16d1-5e15-a12f-b325e9f8db16" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4d4a40a4-8887-524e-8b48-8a24128d12fd" "answer-35881d2a-16d1-5e15-a12f-b325e9f8db16" "answer-d639618d-a932-5b03-8225-fae8a0b21ef5" "answer-32966283-95f9-59c0-9da8-620246a44c9f" "answer-1e4a4287-0b4e-5134-b26d-e720107fbfce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d4a40a4-8887-524e-8b48-8a24128d12fd" :answer/id #uuid "4d4a40a4-8887-524e-8b48-8a24128d12fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-35881d2a-16d1-5e15-a12f-b325e9f8db16" :answer/id #uuid "35881d2a-16d1-5e15-a12f-b325e9f8db16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d639618d-a932-5b03-8225-fae8a0b21ef5" :answer/id #uuid "d639618d-a932-5b03-8225-fae8a0b21ef5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-32966283-95f9-59c0-9da8-620246a44c9f" :answer/id #uuid "32966283-95f9-59c0-9da8-620246a44c9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1e4a4287-0b4e-5134-b26d-e720107fbfce" :answer/id #uuid "1e4a4287-0b4e-5134-b26d-e720107fbfce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ddfb229d-f01d-542c-8a6c-f2e9a5996154" :question/id #uuid "ddfb229d-f01d-542c-8a6c-f2e9a5996154" :question/math-academy-id "q-34639" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, ${a}_{3}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 18 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 18 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{3}=3 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-8{x}_{3}=18 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-3{x}_{3}=9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -8 & 18 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -3 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -3 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{3}=3 \\\\ {x}_{2}=6 \\\\ {x}_{3}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=3.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-2(3)=3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=9.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$ and ${a}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{a}_{1}+6{a}_{2}+3{a}_{3} & =b \\\\ 9\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+6\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 18 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=9\\cdot 6\\cdot 3=162.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0d94e257-45da-5352-bd7b-f0680253dc5b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0d94e257-45da-5352-bd7b-f0680253dc5b" :answer-field/id #uuid "0d94e257-45da-5352-bd7b-f0680253dc5b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-012982fc-c0c6-5360-983d-5c24ecfa5a09" :answer-field/choices ["answer-012982fc-c0c6-5360-983d-5c24ecfa5a09" "answer-3ef56e44-9e80-5352-bfb2-5d35c8c19329" "answer-bcb4217f-2b11-5476-8d7f-3c0e1e75e42b" "answer-65e52e96-8639-5303-a9f5-06fb2d4d391c" "answer-84afc469-3802-566a-b03f-b05bcd3fd37e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-012982fc-c0c6-5360-983d-5c24ecfa5a09" :answer/id #uuid "012982fc-c0c6-5360-983d-5c24ecfa5a09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "162" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3ef56e44-9e80-5352-bfb2-5d35c8c19329" :answer/id #uuid "3ef56e44-9e80-5352-bfb2-5d35c8c19329" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bcb4217f-2b11-5476-8d7f-3c0e1e75e42b" :answer/id #uuid "bcb4217f-2b11-5476-8d7f-3c0e1e75e42b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-65e52e96-8639-5303-a9f5-06fb2d4d391c" :answer/id #uuid "65e52e96-8639-5303-a9f5-06fb2d4d391c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "54" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84afc469-3802-566a-b03f-b05bcd3fd37e" :answer/id #uuid "84afc469-3802-566a-b03f-b05bcd3fd37e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119856 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-435bef4b-b3af-5768-973e-b4aa50ac129d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-435bef4b-b3af-5768-973e-b4aa50ac129d" :question/id #uuid "435bef4b-b3af-5768-973e-b4aa50ac129d" :question/math-academy-id "q-105235" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-9{x}_{2}=-4 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+10{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -9 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 10 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 10 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k-6.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k-6\\,⇒\\,k=6.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a41c8e29-8919-560f-acd3-bb2401f756f5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a41c8e29-8919-560f-acd3-bb2401f756f5" :answer-field/id #uuid "a41c8e29-8919-560f-acd3-bb2401f756f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0e4b9832-4e75-5456-ae0f-c9cbef897a8d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-05a3b4f0-37fc-510b-b782-70713c302e3e" "answer-79384773-3b33-5558-b1a4-01487217122d" "answer-d5b9c506-0e84-558b-99e5-7b80605f2397" "answer-d55768be-caa1-5015-a0a0-51da48688614" "answer-0e4b9832-4e75-5456-ae0f-c9cbef897a8d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-05a3b4f0-37fc-510b-b782-70713c302e3e" :answer/id #uuid "05a3b4f0-37fc-510b-b782-70713c302e3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-79384773-3b33-5558-b1a4-01487217122d" :answer/id #uuid "79384773-3b33-5558-b1a4-01487217122d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d5b9c506-0e84-558b-99e5-7b80605f2397" :answer/id #uuid "d5b9c506-0e84-558b-99e5-7b80605f2397" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d55768be-caa1-5015-a0a0-51da48688614" :answer/id #uuid "d55768be-caa1-5015-a0a0-51da48688614" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0e4b9832-4e75-5456-ae0f-c9cbef897a8d" :answer/id #uuid "0e4b9832-4e75-5456-ae0f-c9cbef897a8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120304 :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc,$ $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨1,5,8⟩$, $c=⟨-1,-1,-3⟩$, and  $u=⟨-3,5,-7⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s-t=-3 \\\\ 5s-t=5 \\\\ 8s-3t=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 8 & -3 & -7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 20 \\\\ 8 & -3 & -7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-8{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 20 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 17\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 17\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=-8,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of $s$ and $t$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc=u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $u$ does *not* lie on the plane $Π.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186117963 :answer-field/correct 17592186117964 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121035 :tutorial/content "Given two vectors $\\mathbf{a}_1$ and $\\mathbf{a}_2,$ the set of all possible linear combinations of $\\mathbf{a}_1$ and $\\mathbf{a}_2$ is\n\n$$\nU = \\left\\{ x_1 \\mathbf{a}_1 + x_2 \\mathbf{a}_2 \\: : \\: x_1,x_2\\in\\mathbb{R} \\right\\}.\n$$\n\nThe set $U$ is also called the **linear span** of $\\mathbf{a}_1$ and $\\mathbf{a}_2,$ and is denoted by $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2 \\}.$ We say that $\\mathbf{a}_1$ and $\\mathbf{a}_2$ are the **generators** of $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2 \\}.$\n\nFor example, let's find the linear span generated by the following vectors:\n![](images/55/55c749dccc54c252b9120f148e383f395c09fb4cd4bec0e1cce8ed441ecb6199.svg)\n\nFrom the definition of linear span, we know that if $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2 \\},$ then $\\mathbf{b}$ must take the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{b} = x_1\\mathbf{a_1} + x_2\\mathbf{a_2}\n$$\n\n for some $x_1,x_2\\in\\mathbb{R}.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & ={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{1} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore the linear span of $\\mathbf{a}_1$ and $\\mathbf{a}_2$ is\n![](images/21/2181b471f34906eeaea7889abbba37c797a2f9624cee455b43b00fc048247cd1.svg)\n\nGeometrically, $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2 \\}$ can be viewed as the plane $\\Pi$ that passes through the origin and is parallel to the vectors $\\mathbf{a}_1$ and $\\mathbf{a}_2,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/d5/d5b202475e0bc3ebb07df1f07bab72e9e74b13a99196c2a8a5adb624a7534a03.png)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-c391d9c3-0c76-5e6f-b0c3-d6b4ee2c37cb" :question/id #uuid "c391d9c3-0c76-5e6f-b0c3-d6b4ee2c37cb"] ["question-c391d9c3-0c76-5e6f-b0c3-d6b4ee2c37cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-105199"] ["question-c391d9c3-0c76-5e6f-b0c3-d6b4ee2c37cb" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$"] ["question-c391d9c3-0c76-5e6f-b0c3-d6b4ee2c37cb" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=3 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=3 \\\\ {x}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}+2{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=3\\cdot 2=6.$"] ["question-c391d9c3-0c76-5e6f-b0c3-d6b4ee2c37cb" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-7847d689-0e36-5ac4-b435-bd1cf0642bc0" :answer-field/id #uuid "7847d689-0e36-5ac4-b435-bd1cf0642bc0"] ["answer-976c158b-03de-5101-af86-c772a635e855" :answer/id #uuid "976c158b-03de-5101-af86-c772a635e855"] ["answer-976c158b-03de-5101-af86-c772a635e855" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-976c158b-03de-5101-af86-c772a635e855" :answer/value "-8"] ["answer-38fb4394-142f-596a-acba-652af141f7ea" :answer/id #uuid "38fb4394-142f-596a-acba-652af141f7ea"] ["answer-38fb4394-142f-596a-acba-652af141f7ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-38fb4394-142f-596a-acba-652af141f7ea" :answer/value "-9"] ["answer-1f1cbd99-3722-58a8-94e3-9b80df51c48b" :answer/id #uuid "1f1cbd99-3722-58a8-94e3-9b80df51c48b"] ["answer-1f1cbd99-3722-58a8-94e3-9b80df51c48b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-1f1cbd99-3722-58a8-94e3-9b80df51c48b" :answer/value "3"] ["answer-1442cd36-01ab-57b5-b752-7b7131e887f9" :answer/id #uuid "1442cd36-01ab-57b5-b752-7b7131e887f9"] ["answer-1442cd36-01ab-57b5-b752-7b7131e887f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-1442cd36-01ab-57b5-b752-7b7131e887f9" :answer/value "4"] ["answer-98c56786-6605-5401-b672-c63cb1cecd33" :answer/id #uuid "98c56786-6605-5401-b672-c63cb1cecd33"] ["answer-98c56786-6605-5401-b672-c63cb1cecd33" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-98c56786-6605-5401-b672-c63cb1cecd33" :answer/value "6"] ["answer-field-7847d689-0e36-5ac4-b435-bd1cf0642bc0" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-7847d689-0e36-5ac4-b435-bd1cf0642bc0" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-7847d689-0e36-5ac4-b435-bd1cf0642bc0" :answer-field/correct "answer-98c56786-6605-5401-b672-c63cb1cecd33"] ["answer-field-7847d689-0e36-5ac4-b435-bd1cf0642bc0" :answer-field/choices "answer-976c158b-03de-5101-af86-c772a635e855"] ["answer-field-7847d689-0e36-5ac4-b435-bd1cf0642bc0" :answer-field/choices "answer-38fb4394-142f-596a-acba-652af141f7ea"] ["answer-field-7847d689-0e36-5ac4-b435-bd1cf0642bc0" :answer-field/choices "answer-1f1cbd99-3722-58a8-94e3-9b80df51c48b"] ["answer-field-7847d689-0e36-5ac4-b435-bd1cf0642bc0" :answer-field/choices "answer-1442cd36-01ab-57b5-b752-7b7131e887f9"] ["answer-field-7847d689-0e36-5ac4-b435-bd1cf0642bc0" :answer-field/choices "answer-98c56786-6605-5401-b672-c63cb1cecd33"] ["question-c391d9c3-0c76-5e6f-b0c3-d6b4ee2c37cb" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-7847d689-0e36-5ac4-b435-bd1cf0642bc0"] [17592186119808 :knowledge-point/questions "question-c391d9c3-0c76-5e6f-b0c3-d6b4ee2c37cb"] ["question-a8427e64-b547-5ecb-a62e-824aa188b632" :question/id #uuid "a8427e64-b547-5ecb-a62e-824aa188b632"] ["question-a8427e64-b547-5ecb-a62e-824aa188b632" :question/math-academy-id "q-34114"] ["question-a8427e64-b547-5ecb-a62e-824aa188b632" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\n$$"] ["question-a8427e64-b547-5ecb-a62e-824aa188b632" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=2 \\\\ {x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}+(-1){a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+(-1)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=2\\cdot (-1)=-2.$"] ["question-a8427e64-b547-5ecb-a62e-824aa188b632" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-283164aa-73de-5dcd-8a69-e6c9e6374abc" :answer-field/id #uuid "283164aa-73de-5dcd-8a69-e6c9e6374abc"] ["answer-4d4a40a4-8887-524e-8b48-8a24128d12fd" :answer/id #uuid "4d4a40a4-8887-524e-8b48-8a24128d12fd"] ["answer-4d4a40a4-8887-524e-8b48-8a24128d12fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-4d4a40a4-8887-524e-8b48-8a24128d12fd" :answer/value "-1"] ["answer-35881d2a-16d1-5e15-a12f-b325e9f8db16" :answer/id #uuid "35881d2a-16d1-5e15-a12f-b325e9f8db16"] ["answer-35881d2a-16d1-5e15-a12f-b325e9f8db16" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-35881d2a-16d1-5e15-a12f-b325e9f8db16" :answer/value "-2"] ["answer-d639618d-a932-5b03-8225-fae8a0b21ef5" :answer/id #uuid "d639618d-a932-5b03-8225-fae8a0b21ef5"] ["answer-d639618d-a932-5b03-8225-fae8a0b21ef5" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d639618d-a932-5b03-8225-fae8a0b21ef5" :answer/value "-3"] ["answer-32966283-95f9-59c0-9da8-620246a44c9f" :answer/id #uuid "32966283-95f9-59c0-9da8-620246a44c9f"] ["answer-32966283-95f9-59c0-9da8-620246a44c9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-32966283-95f9-59c0-9da8-620246a44c9f" :answer/value "4"] ["answer-1e4a4287-0b4e-5134-b26d-e720107fbfce" :answer/id #uuid "1e4a4287-0b4e-5134-b26d-e720107fbfce"] ["answer-1e4a4287-0b4e-5134-b26d-e720107fbfce" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-1e4a4287-0b4e-5134-b26d-e720107fbfce" :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}"] ["answer-field-283164aa-73de-5dcd-8a69-e6c9e6374abc" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-283164aa-73de-5dcd-8a69-e6c9e6374abc" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-283164aa-73de-5dcd-8a69-e6c9e6374abc" :answer-field/correct "answer-35881d2a-16d1-5e15-a12f-b325e9f8db16"] ["answer-field-283164aa-73de-5dcd-8a69-e6c9e6374abc" :answer-field/choices "answer-4d4a40a4-8887-524e-8b48-8a24128d12fd"] ["answer-field-283164aa-73de-5dcd-8a69-e6c9e6374abc" :answer-field/choices "answer-35881d2a-16d1-5e15-a12f-b325e9f8db16"] ["answer-field-283164aa-73de-5dcd-8a69-e6c9e6374abc" :answer-field/choices "answer-d639618d-a932-5b03-8225-fae8a0b21ef5"] ["answer-field-283164aa-73de-5dcd-8a69-e6c9e6374abc" :answer-field/choices "answer-32966283-95f9-59c0-9da8-620246a44c9f"] ["answer-field-283164aa-73de-5dcd-8a69-e6c9e6374abc" :answer-field/choices "answer-1e4a4287-0b4e-5134-b26d-e720107fbfce"] ["question-a8427e64-b547-5ecb-a62e-824aa188b632" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-283164aa-73de-5dcd-8a69-e6c9e6374abc"] [17592186119808 :knowledge-point/questions "question-a8427e64-b547-5ecb-a62e-824aa188b632"] ["question-ddfb229d-f01d-542c-8a6c-f2e9a5996154" :question/id #uuid "ddfb229d-f01d-542c-8a6c-f2e9a5996154"] ["question-ddfb229d-f01d-542c-8a6c-f2e9a5996154" :question/math-academy-id "q-34639"] ["question-ddfb229d-f01d-542c-8a6c-f2e9a5996154" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, ${a}_{3}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 18 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$"] ["question-ddfb229d-f01d-542c-8a6c-f2e9a5996154" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 18 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{3}=3 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-8{x}_{3}=18 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-3{x}_{3}=9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -8 & 18 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -3 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -3 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{3}=3 \\\\ {x}_{2}=6 \\\\ {x}_{3}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=3.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-2(3)=3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=9.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$ and ${a}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{a}_{1}+6{a}_{2}+3{a}_{3} & =b \\\\ 9\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+6\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 18 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=9\\cdot 6\\cdot 3=162.$"] ["question-ddfb229d-f01d-542c-8a6c-f2e9a5996154" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-0d94e257-45da-5352-bd7b-f0680253dc5b" :answer-field/id #uuid "0d94e257-45da-5352-bd7b-f0680253dc5b"] ["answer-012982fc-c0c6-5360-983d-5c24ecfa5a09" :answer/id #uuid "012982fc-c0c6-5360-983d-5c24ecfa5a09"] ["answer-012982fc-c0c6-5360-983d-5c24ecfa5a09" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-012982fc-c0c6-5360-983d-5c24ecfa5a09" :answer/value "162"] ["answer-3ef56e44-9e80-5352-bfb2-5d35c8c19329" :answer/id #uuid "3ef56e44-9e80-5352-bfb2-5d35c8c19329"] ["answer-3ef56e44-9e80-5352-bfb2-5d35c8c19329" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-3ef56e44-9e80-5352-bfb2-5d35c8c19329" :answer/value "18"] ["answer-bcb4217f-2b11-5476-8d7f-3c0e1e75e42b" :answer/id #uuid "bcb4217f-2b11-5476-8d7f-3c0e1e75e42b"] ["answer-bcb4217f-2b11-5476-8d7f-3c0e1e75e42b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-bcb4217f-2b11-5476-8d7f-3c0e1e75e42b" :answer/value "27"] ["answer-65e52e96-8639-5303-a9f5-06fb2d4d391c" :answer/id #uuid "65e52e96-8639-5303-a9f5-06fb2d4d391c"] ["answer-65e52e96-8639-5303-a9f5-06fb2d4d391c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-65e52e96-8639-5303-a9f5-06fb2d4d391c" :answer/value "54"] ["answer-84afc469-3802-566a-b03f-b05bcd3fd37e" :answer/id #uuid "84afc469-3802-566a-b03f-b05bcd3fd37e"] ["answer-84afc469-3802-566a-b03f-b05bcd3fd37e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-84afc469-3802-566a-b03f-b05bcd3fd37e" :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}"] ["answer-field-0d94e257-45da-5352-bd7b-f0680253dc5b" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-0d94e257-45da-5352-bd7b-f0680253dc5b" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-0d94e257-45da-5352-bd7b-f0680253dc5b" :answer-field/correct "answer-012982fc-c0c6-5360-983d-5c24ecfa5a09"] ["answer-field-0d94e257-45da-5352-bd7b-f0680253dc5b" :answer-field/choices "answer-012982fc-c0c6-5360-983d-5c24ecfa5a09"] ["answer-field-0d94e257-45da-5352-bd7b-f0680253dc5b" :answer-field/choices "answer-3ef56e44-9e80-5352-bfb2-5d35c8c19329"] ["answer-field-0d94e257-45da-5352-bd7b-f0680253dc5b" :answer-field/choices "answer-bcb4217f-2b11-5476-8d7f-3c0e1e75e42b"] ["answer-field-0d94e257-45da-5352-bd7b-f0680253dc5b" :answer-field/choices "answer-65e52e96-8639-5303-a9f5-06fb2d4d391c"] ["answer-field-0d94e257-45da-5352-bd7b-f0680253dc5b" :answer-field/choices "answer-84afc469-3802-566a-b03f-b05bcd3fd37e"] ["question-ddfb229d-f01d-542c-8a6c-f2e9a5996154" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-0d94e257-45da-5352-bd7b-f0680253dc5b"] [17592186119808 :knowledge-point/questions "question-ddfb229d-f01d-542c-8a6c-f2e9a5996154"] ["question-435bef4b-b3af-5768-973e-b4aa50ac129d" :question/id #uuid "435bef4b-b3af-5768-973e-b4aa50ac129d"] ["question-435bef4b-b3af-5768-973e-b4aa50ac129d" :question/math-academy-id "q-105235"] ["question-435bef4b-b3af-5768-973e-b4aa50ac129d" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$"] ["question-435bef4b-b3af-5768-973e-b4aa50ac129d" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-9{x}_{2}=-4 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+10{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -9 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 10 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 10 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k-6.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k-6\\,⇒\\,k=6.\n$$"] ["question-435bef4b-b3af-5768-973e-b4aa50ac129d" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-a41c8e29-8919-560f-acd3-bb2401f756f5" :answer-field/id #uuid "a41c8e29-8919-560f-acd3-bb2401f756f5"] ["answer-05a3b4f0-37fc-510b-b782-70713c302e3e" :answer/id #uuid "05a3b4f0-37fc-510b-b782-70713c302e3e"] ["answer-05a3b4f0-37fc-510b-b782-70713c302e3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-05a3b4f0-37fc-510b-b782-70713c302e3e" :answer/value "-4"] ["answer-79384773-3b33-5558-b1a4-01487217122d" :answer/id #uuid "79384773-3b33-5558-b1a4-01487217122d"] ["answer-79384773-3b33-5558-b1a4-01487217122d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-79384773-3b33-5558-b1a4-01487217122d" :answer/value "-8"] ["answer-d5b9c506-0e84-558b-99e5-7b80605f2397" :answer/id #uuid "d5b9c506-0e84-558b-99e5-7b80605f2397"] ["answer-d5b9c506-0e84-558b-99e5-7b80605f2397" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d5b9c506-0e84-558b-99e5-7b80605f2397" :answer/value "3"] ["answer-d55768be-caa1-5015-a0a0-51da48688614" :answer/id #uuid "d55768be-caa1-5015-a0a0-51da48688614"] ["answer-d55768be-caa1-5015-a0a0-51da48688614" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d55768be-caa1-5015-a0a0-51da48688614" :answer/value "5"] ["answer-0e4b9832-4e75-5456-ae0f-c9cbef897a8d" :answer/id #uuid "0e4b9832-4e75-5456-ae0f-c9cbef897a8d"] ["answer-0e4b9832-4e75-5456-ae0f-c9cbef897a8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0e4b9832-4e75-5456-ae0f-c9cbef897a8d" :answer/value "6"] ["answer-field-a41c8e29-8919-560f-acd3-bb2401f756f5" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-a41c8e29-8919-560f-acd3-bb2401f756f5" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-a41c8e29-8919-560f-acd3-bb2401f756f5" :answer-field/correct "answer-0e4b9832-4e75-5456-ae0f-c9cbef897a8d"] ["answer-field-a41c8e29-8919-560f-acd3-bb2401f756f5" :answer-field/choices "answer-05a3b4f0-37fc-510b-b782-70713c302e3e"] ["answer-field-a41c8e29-8919-560f-acd3-bb2401f756f5" :answer-field/choices "answer-79384773-3b33-5558-b1a4-01487217122d"] ["answer-field-a41c8e29-8919-560f-acd3-bb2401f756f5" :answer-field/choices "answer-d5b9c506-0e84-558b-99e5-7b80605f2397"] ["answer-field-a41c8e29-8919-560f-acd3-bb2401f756f5" :answer-field/choices "answer-d55768be-caa1-5015-a0a0-51da48688614"] ["answer-field-a41c8e29-8919-560f-acd3-bb2401f756f5" :answer-field/choices "answer-0e4b9832-4e75-5456-ae0f-c9cbef897a8d"] ["question-435bef4b-b3af-5768-973e-b4aa50ac129d" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-a41c8e29-8919-560f-acd3-bb2401f756f5"] [17592186119856 :knowledge-point/questions "question-435bef4b-b3af-5768-973e-b4aa50ac129d"] [17592186120304 :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc,$ $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨1,5,8⟩$, $c=⟨-1,-1,-3⟩$, and  $u=⟨-3,5,-7⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$"] [17592186120304 :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s-t=-3 \\\\ 5s-t=5 \\\\ 8s-3t=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 8 & -3 & -7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 20 \\\\ 8 & -3 & -7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-8{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 20 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 17\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 17\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=-8,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of $s$ and $t$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc=u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $u$ does *not* lie on the plane $Π.$"] [17592186120304 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [17592186117963 :answer-field/correct 17592186117964] [17592186121035 :tutorial/content "Given two vectors $\\mathbf{a}_1$ and $\\mathbf{a}_2,$ the set of all possible linear combinations of $\\mathbf{a}_1$ and $\\mathbf{a}_2$ is\n\n$$\nU = \\left\\{ x_1 \\mathbf{a}_1 + x_2 \\mathbf{a}_2 \\: : \\: x_1,x_2\\in\\mathbb{R} \\right\\}.\n$$\n\nThe set $U$ is also called the **linear span** of $\\mathbf{a}_1$ and $\\mathbf{a}_2,$ and is denoted by $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2 \\}.$ We say that $\\mathbf{a}_1$ and $\\mathbf{a}_2$ are the **generators** of $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2 \\}.$\n\nFor example, let's find the linear span generated by the following vectors:\n![](images/55/55c749dccc54c252b9120f148e383f395c09fb4cd4bec0e1cce8ed441ecb6199.svg)\n\nFrom the definition of linear span, we know that if $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2 \\},$ then $\\mathbf{b}$ must take the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{b} = x_1\\mathbf{a_1} + x_2\\mathbf{a_2}\n$$\n\n for some $x_1,x_2\\in\\mathbb{R}.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & ={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{1} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore the linear span of $\\mathbf{a}_1$ and $\\mathbf{a}_2$ is\n![](images/21/2181b471f34906eeaea7889abbba37c797a2f9624cee455b43b00fc048247cd1.svg)\n\nGeometrically, $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2 \\}$ can be viewed as the plane $\\Pi$ that passes through the origin and is parallel to the vectors $\\mathbf{a}_1$ and $\\mathbf{a}_2,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/d5/d5b202475e0bc3ebb07df1f07bab72e9e74b13a99196c2a8a5adb624a7534a03.png)"]] "retractions" [[17592186120304 :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π: r = sb + tc$, $t, s ∈ R$, where $b = ⟨1, 5, 8⟩$, $c = ⟨ - 1,-1,-3⟩$, and $u = ⟨ - 3, 5,-7⟩$. In the affirmative case, find the value of $s \\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u = sb + tc$."] [17592186121035 :tutorial/content "Given two vectors $\\mathbf{a}_1$ and $\\mathbf{a}_2,$ the set of all possible linear combinations of $\\mathbf{a}_1$ and $\\mathbf{a}_2$ is\n\n$$\nU = \\left\\{ x_1 \\mathbf{a}_1 + x_2 \\mathbf{a}_2 \\: : \\: x_1,x_2\\in\\mathbb{R} \\right\\}.\n$$\n\nThe set $U$ is also called the **linear span** of $\\mathbf{a}_1$ and $\\mathbf{a}_2,$ and is denoted by $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2 \\}.$ We say that $\\mathbf{a}_1$ and $\\mathbf{a}_2$ are the **generators** of $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2 \\}.$\n\nFor example, let's find the linear span generated by the following vectors:\n![](images/55/55c749dccc54c252b9120f148e383f395c09fb4cd4bec0e1cce8ed441ecb6199.svg)\n\nFrom the definition of linear span, we know that if $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2 \\},$ then $\\mathbf{b}$ must take the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{b} = x_1\\mathbf{a_1} + x_2\\mathbf{a_2}\n$$\n\n for some $x_1,x_2\\in\\mathbb{R}.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & ={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{1} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore the linear span of $\\mathbf{a}_1$ and $\\mathbf{a}_2$ is\n![](images/21/2181b471f34906eeaea7889abbba37c797a2f9624cee455b43b00fc048247cd1.svg)\n\nGeometrically, $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2 \\}$ can be viewed as the plane $\\Pi$ that passes through the origin and is parallel to the vectors $\\mathbf{a}_1$ and $\\mathbf{a}_2,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/d5/d5b202475e0bc3ebb07df1f07bab72e9e74b13a99196c2a8a5adb624a7534a03.png)"]]}]